title: 'pallet-revive: test that operations read and write what they declare'

doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      Adds tests that compare the entries each operation declares with the keys it reads and
      writes, and with the entries it warms in the access list. On both the EVM and PolkaVM
      backends, they cover successful calls (plain, delegate, static and with value), a call to an
      account delegated with EIP-7702, and a contract created by another contract. The tests cover
      the contract creation in both Substrate and Ethereum transactions, and the creation of a
      contract whose code is already stored. They also cover value transfers to a contract, and
      calls to an account that has no code, with and without value.

      Also adds a check that a transfer with dust is charged more than one without.

      No runtime behaviour changes, so nothing needs to be migrated.

crates:
  - name: pallet-revive
    bump: none
